<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stasys Girėnas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1893">1893</a>–<a href="/years/1933">1933</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stasys Girėnas was a Lithuanian-American aviator who with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steponas-darius">Steponas Darius</a> attempted a non-stop flight from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaunas">Kaunas</a> in the aircraft Lituanica in July 1933. After crossing the Atlantic, the plane crashed near Soldin in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> on 17 July, killing both men about 650 kilometres short of Kaunas. Their flight became a national legend in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, commemorated by monuments, a stadium in Kaunas and the ten-litas banknote.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stasys-girenas.jpg" alt="Stasys Girėnas" width="313" height="519" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:S.Girenas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
